1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,239
For decades, we've built the data model backwards.

2
00:00:03,289 --> 00:00:05,859
Here's the fix, and why your AI needs it.

3
00:00:06,309 --> 00:00:09,990
We draw the logical model for business users, in a separate tool.

4
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,245
Developers work backwards from the picture,

5
00:00:12,295 --> 00:00:16,459
so the design drifts from the warehouse, and nobody trusts the diagram.

6
00:00:16,909 --> 00:00:19,303
Then I tried to vibe code data engineering.

7
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:23,441
My AI could read every line of SQL, but it couldn't see the design.

8
00:00:23,491 --> 00:00:26,237
What's the grain? Which keys? It had to guess.

9
00:00:26,687 --> 00:00:30,223
So flip it. Build the logical model for developers first,

10
00:00:30,273 --> 00:00:33,353
and save it in the repo, right next to the SQL.

11
00:00:33,803 --> 00:00:38,587
Each table is one small YAML file, with its grain, columns, types and keys.

12
00:00:38,637 --> 00:00:42,298
A domain file groups the tables and says how they join.

13
00:00:42,748 --> 00:00:47,205
ERD Studio draws those files as a diagram, inside VS Code.

14
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:49,623
Edit either one, and the other updates.

15
00:00:50,073 --> 00:00:52,910
Click View File, and there's the JSON underneath.

16
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:57,798
ERD Studio just renders that file, in one simple, documented format.

17
00:00:57,848 --> 00:01:01,475
Reopen it with ERD Studio, and it's a diagram again.

18
00:01:01,925 --> 00:01:04,218
Logical is the design: what you mean.

19
00:01:04,268 --> 00:01:08,793
Physical is what dbt actually builds, read straight from your project.

20
00:01:09,243 --> 00:01:10,436
Now the best part.

21
00:01:10,486 --> 00:01:11,461
Press Diff.

22
00:01:11,511 --> 00:01:14,885
A renamed column, a wrong type, a missing relationship.

23
00:01:14,935 --> 00:01:17,838
Every mismatch lights up before it ships.

24
00:01:18,288 --> 00:01:22,356
The design change and the SQL change go in the same pull request.

25
00:01:22,406 --> 00:01:25,362
Reviewed together. Tracked together. Shipped together.

26
00:01:25,412 --> 00:01:29,201
It's just common sense. Why did this take us decades to figure out?

27
00:01:29,251 --> 00:01:32,938
And your AI reads the model before it writes a single line.

28
00:01:33,388 --> 00:01:35,233
And the business doesn't lose a thing.

29
00:01:35,283 --> 00:01:39,407
ERD Studio for Confluence renders the same files on a page.

30
00:01:39,457 --> 00:01:41,576
No GitHub account needed.

31
00:01:42,026 --> 00:01:45,520
Not on dbt? Use it for your logical model today.

32
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:47,956
Support for more tools is on the way.

33
00:01:48,406 --> 00:01:50,446
And since the launch, it's taking off.

34
00:01:50,496 --> 00:01:51,766
Come and see why.

35
00:01:53,906 --> 00:01:57,137
ERD Studio. Free, with the source on GitHub.

36
00:01:57,187 --> 00:02:01,110
Search ERD Studio in VS Code. Link in the comments.
